WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:11.232
The Second World War was very hard on the people of Italy.

2
00:00:12.053 --> 00:00:17.715
By the end of the war, some parts of Italy had been nearly destroyed from years of warfare.

3
00:00:19.016 --> 00:00:23.698
Many people, especially the poor, could not see a future there for their families.

4
00:00:25.459 --> 00:00:28.220
One of these people was a young man named Luigi.

5
00:00:30.484 --> 00:00:35.426
Luigi was twenty years old, and he wanted to work, and buy a house for his family.

6
00:00:36.607 --> 00:00:40.949
But jobs were scarce, and many homes around Italy had been demolished.

7
00:00:42.069 --> 00:00:48.172
One day Luigi read an advertisement in the newspaper that told him about the American Dream.

8
00:00:48.192 --> 00:00:53.554
"Come to America and you will find a job and a house," he read.

9
00:00:53.574 --> 00:00:56.656
"In America everyone's dreams come true."

10
00:00:58.896 --> 00:01:03.438
So Luigi packed his bags and kissed his wife and small baby boy good-bye.

11
00:01:03.458 --> 00:01:06.839
"I will go to America and get a job.

12
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:12.002
Then you two can join me and we will buy a house and live a happy life," he

13
00:01:12.102 --> 00:01:13.462
said as he boarded the boat.

14
00:01:13.482 --> 00:01:16.504
"We will achieve the American Dream!"

15
00:01:17.344 --> 00:01:22.846
When Luigi arrived in New York City, there were thousands of other men seeking the American Dream.

16
00:01:24.327 --> 00:01:30.529
Luigi traveled from factory to factory, and construction site to construction site, looking for work.

17
00:01:31.329 --> 00:01:34.150
But again and again employers rejected him.

18
00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:38.731
Sometimes people were polite and apologized.

19
00:01:38.751 --> 00:01:41.452
"Sorry, no jobs today."

20
00:01:42.732 --> 00:01:47.974
But other people treated him very rudely and shouted, "Scram, you dirty immigrant!

21
00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:50.174
Go back to where you came from.

22
00:01:50.394 --> 00:01:52.515
We don't need immigrants around here."

23
00:01:54.035 --> 00:01:59.202
Hungry, lonely, and depressed, Luigi took whatever jobs he could to make money.

24
00:02:00.363 --> 00:02:03.925
For a few weeks, he shined shoes and worked as a sewer cleaner.

25
00:02:05.246 --> 00:02:10.650
But these jobs didn't pay enough to bring over his wife and child, and the jobs were certainly

26
00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:13.091
not Luigi's idea of the American Dream.

27
00:02:14.772 --> 00:02:19.496
Then Luigi heard about a small city with plenty of jobs and opportunities.

28
00:02:20.496 --> 00:02:25.620
The city was Niagara Falls, and it was located about 11 hours from New York City.

29
00:02:26.992 --> 00:02:31.954
So, with just a few pennies in his hand, Luigi boarded a train and headed north.

30
00:02:33.915 --> 00:02:39.357
When he arrived in Niagara Falls, Luigi was amazed at how clean and beautiful it was.

31
00:02:39.377 --> 00:02:43.919
"This is where I will find my American Dream," he declared.

32
00:02:45.239 --> 00:02:47.921
Luigi began searching for a construction job.

33
00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:53.883
But once again, everywhere he went, there were no jobs for immigrants.

34
00:02:54.983 --> 00:02:56.264
Luigi grew desperate.

35
00:02:57.216 --> 00:03:01.098
He had absolutely no money, no friends, and no job.

36
00:03:01.878 --> 00:03:04.099
Would he ever find the American Dream?

37
00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:10.041
One morning he went to yet another construction site and asked for a job.

38
00:03:11.182 --> 00:03:14.043
The foreman said, "Sorry, nothing today."

39
00:03:15.484 --> 00:03:21.486
Luigi became very angry and shouted, "I need a job, and I'm not leaving until I get one!"

40
00:03:22.506 --> 00:03:25.928
With that, Luigi grabbed a shovel and started to work.

41
00:03:26.836 --> 00:03:31.038
He began helping the construction workers dig a long and deep trench.

42
00:03:32.339 --> 00:03:34.981
The astonished foreman watched in disbelief.

43
00:03:35.001 --> 00:03:36.601
"What are you doing?"

44
00:03:37.082 --> 00:03:37.762
he demanded.

45
00:03:37.782 --> 00:03:41.204
"I'm working," replied Luigi.

46
00:03:41.224 --> 00:03:43.926
"If you don't like my work, you don't have to pay me.

47
00:03:44.366 --> 00:03:45.646
But I'm working here today."

48
00:03:47.207 --> 00:03:50.809
Luigi worked harder than any other man all day long.

49
00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:56.972
At the end of the day, Luigi approached the foreman, "So do you like my work?"

50
00:03:58.233 --> 00:03:59.593
"Yes, you do good work."

51
00:04:00.113 --> 00:04:01.274
The foreman acknowledged.

52
00:04:01.294 --> 00:04:06.015
"Then I will come back tomorrow, and you will pay me," said Luigi.

53
00:04:06.835 --> 00:04:09.676
At that all the other workmen started laughing.

54
00:04:10.496 --> 00:04:12.957
They had never witnessed anything like this before.

55
00:04:12.977 --> 00:04:17.278
"You are very bold," remarked one of the men.

56
00:04:17.298 --> 00:04:20.739
"I'm not bold," retorted Luigi.

57
00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:21.819
"I'm just hungry."

58
00:04:23.259 --> 00:04:27.689
The foreman smiled and said, "Okay, Luigi, you have a job.

59
00:04:28.069 --> 00:04:29.870
Come back tomorrow."

60
00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:32.892
Then he reached into this pocket and pulled out some money.

61
00:04:32.912 --> 00:04:35.913
"Here is your money for today.

62
00:04:36.373 --> 00:04:38.994
Go and get something to eat, and buy a new pair of boots."

63
00:04:40.075 --> 00:04:42.676
After that Luigi worked every day.

64
00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:48.879
He was the first to arrive at the construction site in the morning and the last to leave

65
00:04:48.939 --> 00:04:49.339
at night.

66
00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:55.840
Before long he had enough money for his wife and baby to come to America and join him.

67
00:04:56.441 --> 00:05:00.844
Their house was located in an attractive Italian neighborhood in Niagara Falls.

68
00:05:01.625 --> 00:05:04.427
Luigi and his wife eventually had more children.

69
00:05:05.849 --> 00:05:11.874
After a few years, Luigi's family bought a new house that was bigger and very well constructed.

70
00:05:12.374 --> 00:05:19.060
Their neighborhood was near good shops, safe schools, and a new church, which Luigi had helped to build.

71
00:05:19.988 --> 00:05:23.811
His children attended school every day and grew up well.

72
00:05:24.832 --> 00:05:31.458
Many years later Luigi went to the university to attend the graduation ceremony of his youngest son.

73
00:05:32.419 --> 00:05:36.082
During the graduation ceremony, Luigi began to cry.

74
00:05:37.063 --> 00:05:39.004
His wife looked at him in surprise.

75
00:05:39.024 --> 00:05:40.786
"Why are you crying?"

76
00:05:41.346 --> 00:05:41.947
she asked.

77
00:05:41.967 --> 00:05:48.032
"They are tears of happiness," Luigi said.

78
00:05:48.608 --> 00:05:51.813
"Today I have truly achieved the American Dream!"
